Subject: Provide the original empty member-binding selector for native debug emission
Upstream-base: 2c5c51e483b652d178ef06a44b83b07a0f97d2a6

The upstream BindMember primary template passes its declared empty const
BindMemberNoArg selector by reference, which MWCC's inlining removes. Native
O0 and no-inline builds retain a real data relocation. Define that actual
upstream type/symbol exactly once in original nlBind.cpp for native builds.
Do not change Function/BindMember primary templates or their .inl split,
callable selection, argument references, stored capture types, callback
algorithms or logical/physical pool storage. The tag is never a capture field.
Console preprocessing remains unchanged. This is a permanent compiler/link
compatibility provider, not a game behavior workaround or runtime readiness.

diff --git a/src/NL/nlBind.cpp b/src/NL/nlBind.cpp
--- a/src/NL/nlBind.cpp
+++ b/src/NL/nlBind.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,11 @@
 #include "NL/nlBind.h"
+#ifdef MSCHARGED_NATIVE
+#include "NL/nlBindMember.h"
+
+// MWCC removes the unused selector reference while inlining. Native Debug
+// and no-inline builds retain it; supply its actual declared empty type once.
+const BindMemberNoArg bindMemberNoArg = {};
+#endif
 
 #ifndef MSCHARGED_NATIVE
 __declspec(section ".sdata2")
